WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.200
Sadly, 2020 is another busy year for the Tinsel&nbsp;
Town obituaries. From founding fathers of comedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.080
and veteran character actors, to up-and-coming&nbsp;
stars that never got a chance to truly shine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.080
here are the actors we lost in&nbsp;
2020 not yet covered on Looper.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.800
Former child actor Jason Davis died in&nbsp;
February 2020 of a fentanyl overdose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.400
according to the LA County&nbsp;
Medical Examiner. He was 35.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.680
Jason made his debut in the CBS sitcom Dave's&nbsp;
World at age 10 and would go on to appear in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.040
the Chris Farley flop Beverly Hills Ninja as&nbsp;
well as the Jackie Chan-Chris Tucker smash hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.760
Rush Hour while he was still a child. But&nbsp;
his biggest role by far was Mikey Blumberg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:46.480
in Recess — Jason voiced the animated gentle&nbsp;
giant hundreds of times between 1997 and 2003.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.200
“The Young Voices Training Program doesn’t like&nbsp;
the word ‘camp’. They provide opportunities for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.440
aspiring singers to train their voices&nbsp;
in a rigorous, yet supportive, setting.”

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.640
Shortly after being arrested for possession&nbsp;
in 2011, Jason appeared on VH1's Celebrity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.440
Rehab and opened up about his, quote, "scary"&nbsp;
battle with heroin addiction. He's survived by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.640
his brothers, Brandon and Alexander, and two&nbsp;
half-sisters, Isabella and Mariella Rickel.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.320
Newark native Mark Blum, who starred&nbsp;
opposite Madonna in Desperately Seeking Susan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.640
and played Paul Hogan's love rival&nbsp;
in Crocodile Dundee, passed away in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:27.280
March 2020. The stage and screen actor died&nbsp;
after complications from Covid-19. He was 69.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.080
Younger viewers are more likely to recognize Blum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.520
as either Union Bob – the piccolo player in&nbsp;
Amazon's classical music comedy-drama Mozart in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.720
the Jungle – or Mr. Mooney – the bookstore&nbsp;
owner in Netflix's popular stalker show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:46.640
YOU. Blum's final role was Dr. Mark Rutenberg, a&nbsp;
one-off character in Showtime's hit legal series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.720
Billions. He is survived by&nbsp;
his wife, actress Janet Zarish.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:58.320
John Callahan, the soap opera star who played&nbsp;
Edmund Grey on All My Children from 1992 to 2005,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.440
died in March 2020. According to People sources,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.080
Callahan suffered a massive stroke&nbsp;
and did not recover. He was 66.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.120
Callahan married Eva LaRue in 1996,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.160
and the All My Children colleagues had a daughter&nbsp;
named Kaya together before divorcing in 2004.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.280
Callahan is also survived by two step-children&nbsp;
from his previous marriage to Linda Freeman.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.080
Callahan also appeared in over 100&nbsp;
episodes of Days of Our Lives. Other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.960
notable credits include Falcon Crest, Santa&nbsp;
Barbara, Desperate Housewives, and The Bay.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.520
British actress Honor Blackman,&nbsp;
who appeared opposite Sean Connery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:39.440
as iconic Bond girl Pussy Galore in 1964's&nbsp;
Goldfinger, passed away of natural causes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.960
surrounded by family, in April 2020. She was 94.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:43.309
“Isn’t it customary to grant a&nbsp;
condemned man his last request?”

00:02:43.309 --> 00:02:43.440
“You asked for this.”

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:49.440
Blackman rose to prominence in the early 1960s&nbsp;
playing leather-clad super spy Cathy Gale in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:55.520
The Avengers, the 60’s secret agent TV comedy&nbsp;
series. Blackman carried on acting well into her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.400
golden years, but she became better known for her&nbsp;
activism and her political career later in life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.960
She was a card-carrying member of the Liberal&nbsp;
Democrats, and would often speak at party events.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:11.200
Connecticut-born actor Brian Dennehy, best known&nbsp;
for playing dogged small-town sheriff Will Teasle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:17.440
in Sylvester Stallone classic First Blood, died&nbsp;
of natural causes in April 2020. He was 81.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.480
Dennehy won a football scholarship to&nbsp;
Columbia after leaving the Marines in 1963,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.680
and from there he got into Yale,&nbsp;
where he studied dramatic arts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:31.120
After dozens of roles in TV and movies, he&nbsp;
landed a recurring role on Dynasty in 1981,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.680
and his career got another boost the following&nbsp;
year when he played John Rambo's nemesis.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:41.360
Other notable appearances include Ron Howard's&nbsp;
sci-fi Cocoon and the Lawrence Kasdan western&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:47.360
Silverado, both released in 1985. Dennehy made&nbsp;
his overdue Broadway debut in the mid-'90s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.960
and he would later voice the character&nbsp;
Django in Pixar hit Ratatouille.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:55.040
His final appearance was on a 2019&nbsp;
episode of NBC's The Blacklist.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:01.200
Film and TV actor Dimitri Diatchenko, best&nbsp;
known for his turn as reckless tour guide Uri&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:07.440
in the nuclear horror Chernobyl Diaries, passed&nbsp;
away in April 2020. Diatchenko, who was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:13.200
first-generation American of Ukrainian, Swedish,&nbsp;
and Greek heritage, died suddenly at his home in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.720
Florida while recovering from being electrocuted&nbsp;
on the job, his agent confirmed. He was 52.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.680
Diatchenko appeared as a Russian enforcer in&nbsp;
Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.840
Skull and Get Smart, and he played&nbsp;
a similar role in Sons of Anarchy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:32.960
He has numerous other TV and movie credits,&nbsp;
both onscreen and as a voice actor.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:39.520
Bollywood star Irrfan Khan, best known to western&nbsp;
audiences for his turns in Jurassic World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:45.680
Life of Pi, Slumdog Millionaire, and The Amazing&nbsp;
Spider-Man, died in April 2020. The Indian actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:52.640
suffered from a rare neuroendocrine tumor in 2018,&nbsp;
and later succumbed to an infection. He was 53.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:58.080
Khan was born in the northern state of Rajasthan.&nbsp;
He got his start on Indian TV and quickly made the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:04.560
transition to feature length films. He is survived&nbsp;
by his wife, Sutapa, and his sons, Babil and Ayan.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:10.560
Actor and comedian Jerry Stiller passed away&nbsp;
from natural causes in May 2020. His son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:15.200
Hollywood star Ben Stiller, confirmed&nbsp;
his death on Twitter. Stiller was 92.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.240
Stiller made his Broadway debut in 1954,&nbsp;
appearing in the musical comedy The Golden Apple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.720
and his comedy act with wife Anne Meara&nbsp;
was popular throughout the 60’s and beyond.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:28.240
Stiller had roles on TV&nbsp;
sitcoms in the 70’s and 80’s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.120
and in the 90’s began his lengthy stint&nbsp;
on Seinfeld, and later The King of Queens.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:38.320
“When my blood pressure gets too high, the man&nbsp;
on the tape tells me to say ‘Serenity Now!’”

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:39.680
“Are you supposed to yell it?”

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.000
“The man on the tape wasn’t specific.”

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.880
Stiller also popped up in many of his son's&nbsp;
movies over the years, most notably 2001's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:52.720
Zoolander. He also appeared in the sequel, 2016's&nbsp;
Zoolander 2, which was his last feature film.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:59.200
California native Naya Rivera, best known for&nbsp;
playing cheerleader Santana Lopez on the smash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:04.880
hit musical comedy-drama series Glee, died in&nbsp;
July 2020. The singer and actor went boating on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.680
Lake Piru with her four-year-old son, Josey,&nbsp;
and never returned. A search was initiated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:14.160
when Josey was spotted alone on the boat,&nbsp;
and Rivera's body was discovered a few days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:20.240
later. The Ventura County Sheriff's Department&nbsp;
called it a "tragic accident". Rivera was 33.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:24.240
Rivera started out as a child actor,&nbsp;
making her debut on the CBS sitcom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.800
The Royal Family at the age of four. She&nbsp;
appeared on numerous TV shows before Glee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.560
creator Ryan Murphy cast her in what&nbsp;
would become her career-defining role.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:38.000
Ohio-born actor Fred Willard, best known&nbsp;
for his numerous collaborations with actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.520
and filmmaker Christopher Guest, died of&nbsp;
natural causes in May 2020. He was 86.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:49.040
Willard got started in sketch comedy in 1965&nbsp;
and played Jerry Hubbard on the parody talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:54.000
show Fernwood Tonight. His memorable short&nbsp;
appearance in 1984’s This Is Spinal Tap began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.320
his fruitful relationship with Guest, which&nbsp;
would lead to roles in Waiting for Guffman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.680
Best in Show, A Mighty Wind,&nbsp;
and For Your Consideration.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:05.840
Willard was a four-time Emmy nominee.&nbsp;
He passed away just weeks before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.200
premiere of the Netflix series&nbsp;
Space Force, his final role.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.720
Singer and actor Chris Trousdale passed away in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:17.120
June 2020 from complications&nbsp;
from COVID-19. He was 34.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.200
Trousdale achieved Broadway prominence&nbsp;
in Les Misérables, and in the boy band&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:26.080
Dream Street. Many TV appearances followed&nbsp;
on shows like Lucifer and Days of Our Lives.&nbsp;

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.200
His final performance has him&nbsp;
starring as a wedding singer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.880
in the recently released indie romance&nbsp;
flick New York Christmas Wedding.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.760
British character actor Ian Holm,&nbsp;
who played android Ash in Alien and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.840
brought Bilbo Baggins to life in Peter&nbsp;
Jackson's The Lord of the Rings trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:46.480
passed away from a Parkinson's-related&nbsp;
illness in June 2020. He was 88.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:53.680
“I need a holiday...a very long holiday.&nbsp;
And I don’t expect I shall return.”

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.600
Holm was among the first group&nbsp;
of actors recruited to the Royal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:02.160
Shakespeare Company upon its founding&nbsp;
in 1961. In the decades that followed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:06.240
he became a celebrated fixture in British&nbsp;
and American theater at the highest levels.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:11.040
He was nominated for Best Supporting Actor&nbsp;
in 1981 for his role in Chariots of Fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.200
He played Napoleon Bonaparte in Terry&nbsp;
Gilliam's Time Bandits that same year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.520
Prominent parts followed in Brazil, Another&nbsp;
Woman, and The Fifth Element before Holm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.760
debuted as the adventurous Hobbit&nbsp;
Bilbo Baggins, his most iconic role.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:28.720
Two-time Oscar nominee Shirley Knight,&nbsp;
who recurred on Desperate Housewives and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:33.920
appeared in the Paul Blart: Mall Cop&nbsp;
movies, died in April 2020, aged 83.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:39.600
Knight made her TV debut in 1955, and by the&nbsp;
early 60s was a household name in Hollywood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:44.640
She was nominated for a Best Supporting Actress&nbsp;
Oscar for The Dark at the Top of the Stairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.720
and again in Sweet Bird of Youth.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:51.440
After a successful theater stint, Knight&nbsp;
returned to the screen in The Poseidon Adventure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:56.480
and followed this with many TV appearances,&nbsp;
winning 3 of 8 Emmy nominations in the process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:01.200
Her final Emmy nod was in 2006, when she&nbsp;
was recognized for her work as Phyllis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.440
Van de Kamp in Desperate Housewives. Knight&nbsp;
was also the proud owner of a Tony Award.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:10.320
New York-born comedy legend Carl Reiner,&nbsp;
creator of The Dick Van Dyke Show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:15.280
died in his Beverly Hills home surrounded&nbsp;
by family in June 2020. His son, Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:20.320
director Rob Reiner, announced his passing&nbsp;
to the world on Twitter. Carl Reiner was 98.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:22.000
Reiner started working in television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.440
in 1948 and spent the majority of the '50s&nbsp;
bouncing between television and the movies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:31.680
He wouldn't become a household name until the&nbsp;
'60s, the decade of The Dick Van Dyke Show.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:37.120
Other notable credits include Frasier,&nbsp;
House, Seinfeld, Ally McBeal, Mad About You,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:42.000
and the Ocean's Eleven films. Reiner was also&nbsp;
a talented voice actor who played characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:47.280
on Bob's Burgers, Justice League Action,&nbsp;
Family Guy, American Dad, and Toy Story 4.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:53.280
Canadian TV and Broadway actor Nick&nbsp;
Cordero died of COVID-19 in July 2020.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.280 --> 00:10:00.160
He fought the virus for 95 days before passing&nbsp;
away at hospital in Los Angeles. Cordero was 41.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:05.360
Cordero had many theater roles because achieving&nbsp;
his first full Broadway production in 2012.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.400
He played Cheech in Bullets Over Broadway in 2014,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:11.760
picking up a Tony nomination for&nbsp;
his work in the jukebox musical.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:16.960
The Ontario native also worked on TV’s&nbsp;
Queer as Folk, Lilyhammer, and Law &amp; Order:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.040
Special Victims Unit, and in feature&nbsp;
films A Stand Up Guy and Going in Style.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:27.680
Hollywood legend Olivia de Havilland, the last&nbsp;
surviving star of 1939's Gone with the Wind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:32.240
passed away from natural&nbsp;
causes in July 2020 at age 104.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:38.480
During the classic film era, de Havilland starred&nbsp;
opposite Errol Flynn in no fewer than eight films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:43.600
though her role as Melanie in Gone with the Wind&nbsp;
was her most famous. The Best Picture winner is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:48.720
still considered the most financially successful&nbsp;
film of all time after inflation adjustments.

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:51.760
De Havilland went on to win&nbsp;
Best Actress statuettes for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:55.520
1946's To Each His Own and 1949's The Heiress.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:00.080
Japanese film and TV star Haruma&nbsp;
Miura, who starred in the live action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:06.560
adaptation Attack on Titan, died in July&nbsp;
2020 in a possible suicide. The actor was 30.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:12.320
Miura was a former child actor, who worked in&nbsp;
TV through his teens. Miura flitted between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:15.840
movies and television in the decade that&nbsp;
followed, receiving praise for his work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:21.680
in the aviation epic The Eternal Zero, and&nbsp;
soon after the two Attack on Titan movies.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.800
If you or anyone you know&nbsp;
is having suicidal thoughts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:32.240
please call the National Suicide Prevention&nbsp;
Lifeline at 1-800-273-TALK (8255).

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:37.520
Mustachioed character actor Wilford&nbsp;
Brimley passed away in August 2020&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:41.200
after a struggle with diabetes&nbsp;
and kidney disease. He was 85.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:46.400
Brimley made his big screen breakthrough as&nbsp;
a foreman in 1979's The China Syndrome. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:52.400
impressed in Sydney Pollack's Absence of Malice In&nbsp;
1981, worked under John Carpenter in the seminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:59.120
sci-fi horror The Thing in 1982, and starred as&nbsp;
rejuvenated geriatric Ben Luckett in Ron Howard's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:04.720
Cocoon in 1985. Brimley became a fixture on&nbsp;
American television in the '80s and '90s as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:09.840
the no-nonsense Quaker Oats guy, and became a&nbsp;
meme for his TV ads for diabetes test strips.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:17.280
Dame Diana Rigg, Bond girl Tracy di Vicenzo&nbsp;
in On Her Majesty's Secret Service and Olenna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:23.040
Tyrell in Game of Thrones, passed away in&nbsp;
September 2020. The acting legend was 82.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:28.160
“It’s a rare enough thing: a man&nbsp;
who lives up to his reputation.”

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:35.360
Rigg began her career as a stage actor in&nbsp;
1959. She made her screen debut that same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:40.640
year in a made-for-TV version of A Midsummer&nbsp;
Night's Dream, then became a household name as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:46.800
secret agent Emma Peel in the classic spy show&nbsp;
The Avengers. Now a fashion icon and sex symbol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:51.360
Rigg portrayed the only Bond&nbsp;
Girl to marry 007 in 1969.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:54.640
Rigg returned to international&nbsp;
prominence in Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:59.920
and her final feature film, Edgar Wright's&nbsp;
Last Night in Soho, is set to arrive in 2021.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:05.040
Anglo-French actor Michael Lonsdale,&nbsp;
who starred in The Day of the Jackal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:10.960
and played Bond villain Hugo Drax in&nbsp;
Moonraker, died in September 2020. He was 89.

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:16.480
Lonsdale studied painting before becoming an&nbsp;
actor, making his stage debut at the age of 24&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:21.280
and his first screen appearances in the 1950’s.&nbsp;
Following blockbuster roles in the 70’s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:27.120
he would go on to appear alongside Robert De Niro&nbsp;
and Jean Reno in the 1998 action flick Ronin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:32.880
and later played the character Papa in Steven&nbsp;
Spielberg's historical thriller Munich in 2005.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:36.320
Lonsdale's final film was 2016 sci-fi Sculpt.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:39.680
Singer and actress Helen Reddy,&nbsp;
who became synonymous with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:44.000
feminist movement and appeared in the&nbsp;
films Airport 1975 and Pete's Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:48.320
died in September 2020. The&nbsp;
Australian Grammy winner was 78.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:52.240
In her career, Reddy would record&nbsp;
over a dozen top 40 singles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:56.240
though she will always be remembered&nbsp;
for "I Am Woman," her feminist anthem.

00:13:56.240 --> 00:14:00.800
Reddy played Sister Ruth in airborne&nbsp;
thriller Airport 1975 the year after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:05.600
winning her first Grammy, and in 1977 she&nbsp;
took on the role of Nora in Pete's Dragon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:11.280
Notable TV credits include Fantasy Island, The&nbsp;
Jeffersons, and Diagnosis Murder. I Am Woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:16.000
a biopic about Reddy's rise to stardom,&nbsp;
premiered just a month before her death.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:21.280
Actor Clark Middleton passed away in October&nbsp;
2020 after suffering from West Nile virus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:24.720
The veteran actor and&nbsp;
disabilities advocate was 63.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:29.440
Middleton lived with Rheumatoid Arthritis for&nbsp;
most of his life, but he never let it stop him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:35.120
from pursuing his passion. He made his stage debut&nbsp;
in 1983 and developed into a dependable big screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:41.280
actor. Middleton worked with Quentin Tarantino&nbsp;
on Kill Bill Vol. 2, Ang Lee in Taking Woodstock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:47.600
Bong Joon Ho in Snowpiercer, David Lynch in&nbsp;
Twin Peaks: The Return, and Alejandro Iñárritu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:52.960
in Best Picture winner Birdman. Middleton was&nbsp;
also regularly seen on many different TV shows.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:57.200
Veteran actress and dancer Marge&nbsp;
Champion, who starred in a series of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:03.440
musicals opposite her husband in the 1950s,&nbsp;
passed away in October 2020 at the age 101.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:08.240
In the 1930's, Champion served as the model&nbsp;
for Walt Disney’s titular character in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:13.280
Snow White and the Seven Dwarves. She also&nbsp;
modeled the Blue Fairy in 1940’s Pinocchio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:16.640
Hyacinth Hippo in Fantasia,&nbsp;
and Mr. Stork in Dumbo.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:21.440
Champion made her Broadway debut in 1945, and&nbsp;
would become a movie star the following decade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.440
with a string of MGM musicals. Champion&nbsp;
would later scoop an Emmy Award for her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:31.120
choreography work on the critically acclaimed&nbsp;
1975 telefilm Queen of the Stardust Ballroom.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:35.760
Sean Connery, the Scottish movie icon&nbsp;
best known for originating the role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:40.640
of James Bond on the big screen,&nbsp;
died in October 2020 at age 90.

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:47.440
Connery rose to prominence in 1961, in the BBC's&nbsp;
Anna Karenina. The former model made his debut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:54.480
as 007 in Dr. No in 1963. Connery became a&nbsp;
globally recognized star, and his influence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:59.760
grew with every subsequent installment.&nbsp;
Connery appeared in 8 Bond films in total.

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:02.160
“I admire your luck, Mister…?”

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:06.640
“Bond. James Bond.”

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:09.680
Post-Bond, Connery appeared&nbsp;
in films like Highlander,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.720
The Untouchables, Indiana&nbsp;
Jones and the Last Crusade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:17.840
The Hunt for Red October and The Rock. He was&nbsp;
knighted in 2000, and would appear in his final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:22.320
live action film, the widely-panned The League&nbsp;
of Extraordinary Gentlemen, three years later.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:27.600
Actor Eddie Hassell, who played Clay in the&nbsp;
Best Picture nominee The Kids Are All Right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:30.640
and Apple employee Chris Espinosa in Jobs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:37.200
died in November 2020. Hassell was fatally wounded&nbsp;
in a robbery gone tragically wrong. He was 30.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:42.560
Hassell landed his first significant role in&nbsp;
2005, securing the part of Phil Nance in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:47.760
Lake Bell-led sci-fi series Surface, which&nbsp;
led to more prominent roles in film. Hassell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:52.640
was also known for Devious Maids, on which he&nbsp;
recurred as the wrongfully convicted Eddie Suarez.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:58.560
Bert Belasco, best known for playing Charles&nbsp;
Whitmore in the BET sitcom Let's Stay Together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:03.840
passed away in November 2020. Belasco was&nbsp;
pronounced dead at a hotel in Virginia of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:08.720
a likely aneurysm, according to his&nbsp;
father’s report to TMZ. He was 38.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:11.600
After early work in improv and&nbsp;
video game vocal performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:17.040
Belasco appeared in an episode of House. He&nbsp;
went on to become a regular on American TV,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:21.840
recurring on the baseball dramedy Pitch and the&nbsp;
Jim Carrey-produced I'm Dying Up Here. Other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:27.200
notable appearances include Justified, Key and&nbsp;
Peele, NCIS: New Orleans, and American Princess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:32.400
though Belasco will undoubtedly be remembered&nbsp;
for his 52-episode stint on Let's Stay Together.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:37.600
Star of the stage and screen Lawrence Clayton,&nbsp;
who made his Broadway debut as part of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:43.760
replacement cast of Dreamgirls, died in November&nbsp;
2020 after a battle with cancer. He was 64.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:48.000
Clayton was a regular in New York’s theater&nbsp;
scene. He made his bow as C.C. White in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:52.720
Dreamgirls in 1981 and went on to appear&nbsp;
in a number of other Broadway musicals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.840
He appeared in the 2015&nbsp;
revival of The Color Purple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.840 --> 00:18:01.520
and the Oprah Winfrey-produced show won the Tony&nbsp;
Award for Best Revival of a Musical. Clayton also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:06.480
toured with productions of Jesus Christ Superstar&nbsp;
and Les Miserables during his days on the stage.

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:11.440
As for TV, Clayton made his screen debut&nbsp;
in a 1989 episode of The Equalizer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:17.040
later appearing on Deadline, Law &amp; Order: Criminal&nbsp;
Intent, As the World Turns, The Big C, Homeland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:22.480
Law &amp; Order: Special Victims Unit, and the CBS&nbsp;
Sherlock Holmes show Elementary. Clayton made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:28.720
his final appearance in a 2019 episode of&nbsp;
Netflix's groundbreaking LGBTQ drama Pose.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:34.400
Compton native Tommy "Tiny" Lister, best known&nbsp;
for playing neighborhood bully Deebo in the Friday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:40.000
films, passed away in December 2020. The actor&nbsp;
and former wrestler was found unresponsive at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:46.560
his California apartment, Variety confirmed, after&nbsp;
reporting COVID-19-like symptoms. Lister was 62.

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:52.000
Lister was a prolific character actor who had well&nbsp;
over 200 credits to his name when he died. He made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:58.160
his debut as a football player in a 1984 episode&nbsp;
of ABC sitcom Webster and would have a stint in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:02.800
professional wrestling before establishing himself&nbsp;
as a go-to tough guy in Hollywood. He played a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:07.680
bail agent in Quentin Tarantino's Jackie Brown&nbsp;
and a tattooed prisoner in Christopher Nolan's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:11.920
The Dark Knight, but it was the role of Deebo&nbsp;
that earned him a place in pop culture history.

